Name: isListening

Type: function

Syntax: isListening()

Summary:
Returns true if the speech recognition engine is currently active,
false otherwise.

Introduced: 1.1.0

OS: mac

Platforms: desktop

Example:
-- Only register commands if not already listening
if not isListening() then
    registerVoiceCommand "open stack"
    startListening
end if

Example:
-- Toggle listening on a button click
if isListening() then
    stopListening
    set the label of me to "Start Listening"
else
    startListening
    set the label of me to "Stop Listening"
end if

Returns: true if <startListening> has been called and the engine is
running; false if the engine has not been started or was stopped with
<stopListening>.

Description:
Use <isListening> to query the current state of the speech recognition
engine without attempting to start or stop it. The function reflects the
state set by <startListening> and <stopListening>.

On platforms where speech recognition is not yet implemented (Windows,
Linux), <isListening> always returns false.

References: startListening (command), stopListening (command),
registerVoiceCommand (command), voiceCommand (message)

Tags: speech, voice
